Architecture

    Java Swing desktop app. One local JVM. Three-layer MVC, dependency direction strictly
    downward — presentacio → domini → persistencia.contract. Domain layer imports no Swing,
    no JDBC. Look & Feel is FlatLaf 3.7.2 (Nimbus was dropped in the 2026-10 UI redesign).

    - src/presentacio (86 files, 13 500 lines) — Swing panels, controllers, dialogs, renderers,
      gallery, plus 35 local SVG icons. Split *Panel design vs *Control logic.
    - src/domini (22 files, 2 163 lines) — ControladorDomini singleton facade, 67 public
      methods, all one-line delegations to 7 role delegates (DelegatLlibre, DelegatPrestatgeria,
      TagDelegate, DelegatPrestec, DelegatEstadistiques, DelegatCopiaSeguretat,
      NamedEntityDelegate) over StateContext.
    - src/persistencia (37 files, 3 253 lines) — contract/ 11 interfaces, dao/ 8, row/ 9 records,
      internal/ 8. One ControladorPersistencia singleton, every method synchronized.
    - src/herramienta (44 files, 5 675 lines) — config, i18n, IO, CSV, text, theming
      (UITheme palette + Tokens metrics), OpenLibrary client.
    - src/main (2 files, 195 lines) — bootstrap. DB open runs parallel to theme install on a
      daemon thread.

    Two shared states, must not conflate:
    - domini.facade.StateContext — domain-side, one lock monitor, withLock / withLockReturning,
      defensive snapshotAll(), atomic replaceAll().
    - presentacio.util.EstatVistaBiblioteca — UI-side, EDT-confined, not thread-safe.

    Write-through persistence: in-memory state plus DB write on every mutation. Schema
    versioned via schema_version table, 39 migrations in ConnexioServidor.

    Build is plain Makefile + javac. No Maven/Gradle. build/maven-legacy/pom.xml is an
    abandoned attempt, still on disk.

    Two web prototypes exist (Biblioteca.html + components.jsx React/Babel CDN;
    .config/ide/vscode-java-bin/web/ vanilla JS). Neither is wired to the Java build.

    Features

    Catalogue with title, authors, ISBN-10/13 with check digit, year, rating 0-10, price,
    cover blob, notes, per-locale titles. Covers auto-imported from OpenLibrary by ISBN,
    stored as BLOB in DB.

    Unlimited shelves, each book carrying own rating and read-state per shelf. Free-form tags.
    Real-time search across title, author, ISBN, description, notes. Composable filters
    (rating, year, language, format, shelf, tag, read-state).

    Loans with returns and overdue detection. Reading progress with progress-bar cell.
    Statistics: per-shelf averages, read percentages, top authors, reading pace.

    Import CSV (native, Goodreads, LibraryThing), JSON, Calibre metadata.db. Export CSV, JSON,
    HTML, PDF. SQL backup with validated restore plus automatic pre-restore safety copy.

    UI: 4 themes (clar/fosc/sepia/ocean), 3 font sizes (small 11 / medium 13 / large 16),
    3 locales (ca/es/en), table and gallery modes, keyboard shortcuts, barcode scan station.

