    Risks

    1. Eager full-table load — MEDIUM. ControladorDomini constructor loads the entire llibre
       table unconditionally, contradicting the large-library pagination path it also builds.
    2. No connection pool — MEDIUM. Every DB call opens and closes a connection, and one global
       synchronized lock serialises all of them, bulk imports included.
    3. Statistics tab build on the EDT — MEDIUM. The aggregation itself moved into a
       SwingWorker, but the dialog still assembles tables and charts on the EDT.
    4. Cover BLOBs excluded from SQL backup. Restore loses covers; re-download required. Format
       decision, documented, not a bug.
    5. i18n newline convention split. CSV keys use literal \n (2 chars) and render as literal
       text; 5 manual I18n.java keys use a real newline. Inconsistent inside one table. Needs
       product decision, not a point fix.
    6. I18n.java is generated but carries 5 hand-written keys; the generator now emits the Java
       from scripts/i18n_java_template.java.tmpl. Regenerating drops the manual keys. Guarded by
       docs/agent/MISTAKES.md; git checkout -- after any exploratory regen.
    7. Backlog file missing. docs/agent/AGENTS.md and .opencode/agent/loop.md both name tot.txt
       at repo root as source of truth for open work. No such file — it lives in
       docs/code-review/tot.txt.
    8. Agent instructions stale. .opencode/agent/loop.md names root /home/j/Documents/DeV/Biblioteca
       (actual /home/j/projects/Biblioteca), classes MainFrameControl / ServerConect /
       MostrarBibliotecaControl (actual PanelMarcPrincipal / ConnexioServidor /
       ControladorMostrarBiblioteca), and treats src/listener/ as a top-level package.
    9. Repo bloat. .git 405M, packaging/ 182M (323 tracked files — bundled Temurin JRE committed),
